eration). No info on decision quality, adaptability.\n\nD: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (decision quality, technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility). Concerns: know-it-all (crew cooperation), hot temper (stress, communication). No info on reliability, technical competence specifics.\n\nWe need to decide recommendation. C is strong but communication issues may be serious for long-distance crew. B has strong reliability and stress but communication issues (nasty remarks) also serious. A has strong technical and leadership but unknown reliability and stress. D has strong problem solving and responsibility but hot temper and know-it-all.\n\nWhich candidate overall best? Possibly Candidate B? But nasty remarks could be severe. C's egocentric and communication difficulty also severe. A's show-off and not open to new ideas also problematic. D's hot temper also problematic.\n\nWe need to weigh. Perhaps Candidate B's conscientiousness and stress handling outweigh memory issue and remarks? But remarks are about colleagues, could affect crew cooperation. C's communication difficulty also affects crew. Which is worse? Hard to decide.\n\nWe could ask another panel member for more info on Candidate B's communication style or on Candidate D's temperament. But we can also make an argument now.\n\nWe need to give a vote. Could we shift recommendation to Candidate B? Provide reasoning: B's reliability and stress handling are critical, and his technical skills are good. The memory issue is minor, and remarks could be mitigated with training. Compared to C's egocentric and unwillingness to further education, which may be more entrenched.\n\nThus we could change vote to B. Or we could keep C but note concerns.\n\nGiven we need to move discussion forward, we could present concerns about C and propose B as alternative. So we can change vote to B.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's points. Provide evidence from our notes.\n\nThus public message: I agree C strong but communication concerns; I think B may be better overall because of conscientiousness, stress handling, weather assessment, and computer skills, while his memory issue is less critical than C's egocentric attitude. So I vote for B.\n\nLet's produce."}
