r Candidate B. The last turn was Agent 2 (the user is now Agent 2's turn). Actually the last public message was from Agent 2 (the assistant) recommending B. Now it's Agent 3's turn (we). We need to respond, referencing prior discussion, maybe bring up D again, or reinforce B, or possibly shift. According to shared mental model, we still lack D info. We could ask a question about D's reliability or adaptability, but we already asked earlier and got no info. Could ask about D's professional communication style again? Already asked. So maybe we can bring up D's known strengths and concerns, compare to B, and maintain B. Provide explicit facts: D responds to unexpected events adequately, solves problems extremely well, can concentrate very well, takes responsibility seriously, but is regarded as a know-it-all, hot temper, moody, loner. These affect crew cooperation and communication. So B still best.\n\nThus we produce public message: I agree with Agent 2, maintain B, note D's lack of reliability evidence and communication concerns, and note that B's issues are more manageable.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
